# BlockingBear backend development and Docker Compose configuration
#
# Copying is automated for installations; run from the repository root:
#
#   sh scripts/init-env.sh
#
# This one ignored file intentionally has two consumers:
#
# - a backend process started from source loads every active value below;
# - Docker Compose reads the file for interpolation, but passes only variables
#   explicitly declared in docker-compose.yaml. Development values such as
#   DATABASE_URL, PII_MODEL_DIR, workers and CORS do not override the container.
#
# scripts/init-env.sh preserves every existing entry and fills only the two
# mandatory Compose secrets. It never prints secret material. Never commit
# backend/.env. OpenRouter credentials never belong here: the management key
# is entered in the application's setup wizard after the first start.

# --- Backend source development: required -----------------------------------
# These three active values let app.config start correctly from source. They are
# ignored by the supported Compose deployment, whose image defines its own values.

# Parallel document workers. Each loads a separate copy of the PII model.
BLOCKINGBEAR_N_WORKERS=1

# Vite development origins. Use an empty value when serving frontend and backend
# from the same origin.
BLOCKINGBEAR_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Relative to backend/, matching the versioned checkpoint download directory.
PII_MODEL_DIR=models/rizzo-pii-0.3B-v1.5.0

# --- Backend source development: optional -----------------------------------
# Empty or absent values use the defaults documented in backend/app/config.py.

# Total CPU threads available to PII inference. Default: host cores minus one.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CPU_THREADS=7

# Application data directory. Default in source development: backend/data.
# Prefer an absolute path when overriding it.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/blockingbear-data

# Database used by a backend started from source. Absent = SQLite inside
# BLOCKINGBEAR_DATA_DIR. Compose always constructs its own PostgreSQL URL.
#DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://blockingbear:password@127.0.0.1:5432/blockingbear

# Explicit LibreOffice executable. Absent = automatic discovery.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SOFFICE_PATH=/usr/bin/soffice

# Local code-interpreter runtime and limits.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_ENGINE=auto
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_IMAGE=blockingbear-sandbox:1
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_POOL=2
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_MAX=4
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_IDLE_MIN=60
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_MEM=2g
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_EXEC_TIMEOUT=120
#BLOCKINGBEAR_SANDBOX_MAX_ITER=12

# Local web-search browser settings. Compose supplies its own Camofox URL and key.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9377
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_API_KEY=
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_IMAGE=ghcr.io/redf0x1/camofox-browser
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_PORT=9377
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_MEM=2g
#BLOCKINGBEAR_WEB_PAGE_MAX_CHARS=25000
#BLOCKINGBEAR_WEB_SEARCH_URL=https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q={q}

# Diagnostics and OpenRouter-compatible test endpoint overrides.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
#BLOCKINGBEAR_OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# --- Mandatory Docker Compose secrets ---------------------------------------
# Generated automatically by scripts/init-env.sh. Never commit real values.
BLOCKINGBEAR_PG_PASSWORD=
BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- PostgreSQL (optional overrides) -----------------------------------------
# The supported Compose deployment always uses its PostgreSQL service. Compose
# constructs DATABASE_URL internally from these values.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_PG_USER=blockingbear
#BLOCKINGBEAR_PG_DB=blockingbear
#BLOCKINGBEAR_PG_PORT=5432

# --- Host data and model paths (optional overrides) --------------------------
# Relative paths are resolved from the repository root. The defaults match the
# locations prepared and checked by scripts/preflight.sh.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_DATA_DIR_HOST=./data
#BLOCKINGBEAR_MODEL_DIR_HOST=./backend/models/rizzo-pii-0.3B-v1.5.0

# Internal container path for application data. Normally do not change this.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_DATA_DIR=/srv/blockingbear/data

# --- Required code-interpreter socket ---------------------------------------
# preflight.sh detects and writes these non-secret values so later Compose
# commands work from a new shell. The GID is probed inside a uid 1000 container,
# because desktop VM mount layers can map it differently from the host inode.
# Linux and integrated WSL2 normally use /var/run/docker.sock; macOS Docker
# Desktop may use $HOME/.docker/run/docker.sock.
BLOCKINGBEAR_DOCKER_SOCKET=
BLOCKINGBEAR_DOCKER_GID=

# --- NVIDIA build override ---------------------------------------------------
# GPU selection is not enabled here. preflight.sh adds
# docker-compose.nvidia.yaml when NVIDIA passthrough works. This optional value
# only overrides the verified PyTorch index declared by that Compose file.
#BLOCKINGBEAR_TORCH_INDEX=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126

# --- Camofox administration (optional) ---------------------------------------
#BLOCKINGBEAR_CAMOFOX_ADMIN_KEY=
#BLOCKINGBEAR_VNC_PASSWORD=
